{"custom_id":"s-ap_calculus_bc-m05-k1","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCxFnqibnWDTQPza9ExZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The speed is least at **t = 1.000** (choice index 2).\n\n1. Speed is |v(t)|, and the speed squared is S(t) = (t² − 4t + 2)² + (2t − 3)². S is smallest exactly where the speed is smallest, so I minimized S.\n2. Differentiate: S′(t) = 2(t² − 4t + 2)(2t − 4) + 4(2t − 3).\n3. Set S′(t) = 0 and divide by 4: (t² − 4t + 2)(t − 2) + (2t − 3) = 0.\n4. Expanding gives t³ − 6t² + 12t − 7 = 0.\n5. t = 1 is a root. Factoring gives (t − 1)(t² − 5t + 7) = 0. The quadratic has discriminant 25 − 28 = −3 < 0, so t = 1 is the only critical point.\n6. Check the critical point and the endpoints:\n   - S(0) = 2² + (−3)² = 13\n   - S(1) = (−1)² + (−1)² = 2\n   - S(4) = 2² + 5² = 29\n\nThe smallest value is at t = 1, where the speed is √2."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W6F7JX7xsnWjLUhf3HjJ2y","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"1","choice_index":2,"final_answer":"1.000","brief_reasoning":"Speed^2 derivative gives (t-1)(t^2-5t+7)=0, so t=1 is the only critical point. Speed^2 is 2 at t=1, 13 at t=0 and 29 at t=4, so the minimum is at t=1.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568},"output_tokens":852,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":277},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568},"output_tokens":852,"output_tokens_d